{"name":"Nuclear Throne","hex":"#00de00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nuclear","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the nucleus of an atom. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Involving energy released by nuclear reactions (fission, fusion, radioactive decay)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Nuclear power.","Nuclear weapon"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nuclear"},{"term":"throne","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An impressive seat used by a monarch, often on a raised dais in a throne room and reserved for formal occasions.","Leadership, particularly the position of a monarch."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place on a royal seat; to enthrone.","To place in an elevated position; to give sovereignty or dominion to; to exalt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/throne"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nuclear Throne","blocks":[{"text":"Nuclear Throne is a roguelike top-down shoot 'em up with bullet hell elements developed by the Dutch indie studio Vlambeer. Set in a post-apocalyptic wasteland populated by mutants, the player fights through procedurally generated levels, collecting weapons and radiation-based \"mutations\" in an attempt to reach the titular Nuclear Throne. The game began as a game jam prototype called Wasteland Kings in February 2013 and was developed largely in public, with most of its two-and-a-half-year production livestreamed on Twitch in a process the studio called \"performative development\". After more than two years in Early Access, it was released for Linux, Windows, OS X, PlayStation 4 and PlayStation Vita on December 5, 2015, and was later ported to Nintendo Switch (2019) and Xbox One (2021)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Nuclear_Throne_icon.png/330px-Nuclear_Throne_icon.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_Throne","wikidata":"Q21775834"},{"title":"Throne","blocks":[{"text":"A throne is the seat of state of a potentate or dignitary, especially the seat occupied by a sovereign on state occasions; or the seat occupied by a pope or bishop on ceremonial occasions. \"Throne\" in an abstract sense can also refer to the monarchy itself, an instance of metonymy, and is also used in many expressions such as \"the power behind the throne\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Gamla_Stan%2C_S%C3%B6dermalm%2C_Stockholm%2C_Sweden_-_panoramio_%28225%29.jpg/330px-Gamla_Stan%2C_S%C3%B6dermalm%2C_Stockholm%2C_Sweden_-_panoramio_%28225%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Throne","wikidata":"Q189233"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Nuclear_Throne_screenshot_06.png/500px-Nuclear_Throne_screenshot_06.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Nuclear_Throne_screenshot_06.png/500px-Nuclear_Throne_screenshot_06.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gameplay screenshot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANuclear_Throne_screenshot_06.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Vlambeer_at_GDC_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Vlambeer_at_GDC_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Vlambeer_at_GDC_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Vlambeer_at_GDC_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rami Ismail and Jan Willem Nijman at GDC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVlambeer_at_GDC_(cropped).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Thron_Salamis.JPG/500px-Thron_Salamis.JPG?utm_s